WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.980
This is a work of fiction based on research into the period in which it is set. The people,
 organization, laws, and names that appear in it have no relation to any in the real world.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:45.000
Dark Wings

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:57.350
Mr. Maeda?

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.850
Oh, my, Colonel Maeda.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:03.440
My apologies; I had no idea
you were still alive.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.110
I am the new commander appointed
to lead Special Forces Unit 16,

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:10.480
Rufus Glenn.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:13.860
Well then...

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.620
...take your time.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.420
Misaki.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.250
I will eliminate vampires.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.630
Mr. Maeda!

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.140
Defrott!

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.510
You must know

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.600
this isn't your cue!

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.520
Watch out!

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.350
Defrott!

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.320
Stay back!

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.090
We're vampires. I'm one, and so is he.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.150
Wh...

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.530
Why?

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.500
How could you...

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.380
...do that to a child?

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.050
Misaki.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.950
Hey!

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.530
Hang on!

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.700
Morning.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.250
Good morning.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.080
Is the big kite done?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.630
You can't rush it.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:34.340
I'm a city man; I can't help it.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:38.670
It's not a bowl of noodles.
They can't build it that fast.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.010
When it is ready, give Goemon a look at it.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.010
Soon enough.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.180
Thanks!

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.310
Well, I'll be seeing you.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.890
♪ High, high flies the kite... ♪

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:51.100
He has such strange tastes.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.110
You're pulling too hard.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.940
Sorry.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.900
Welcome back, Mr. Tenmanya.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.120
Oh, Mr. Tenmanya!

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.370
Don't worry. This is nothing.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.160
It's not getting better.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.080
Because I'm human.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.840
Why is a human helping vampires?

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:18.170
Because I've been helped before.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.880
I'll bandage it.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:27.350
The young master was born
to a Japanese person and a foreigner.

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:28.720
Huh?

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.980
Among humans, he was bullied

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.230
and despised.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:35.900
We were his only playmates.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.400
TENMANYA

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.660
Let's hurry!

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:46.580
Where to, Young Master?

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.370
The Sumida River fireworks.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.000
Take care of him.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.040
Sure.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.920
Young Master.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.710
I know; I'll cover up.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.110
What do you think, Shin?

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.740
Shin?

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.120
It's dark, so It'll be fine.

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:49.100
Where'd he go?

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.270
Come out, monster!

00:06:58.810 --> 00:06:59.900
Shin?

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:02.190
That was the young master's voice.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:03.570
From the grounds.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.120
Shin!

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.490
Stop!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.250
The previous master rescued me

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:18.080
and let me survive until now.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.840
If I can repay him...

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:32.640
You've got to be careful, Shin.

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:46.990
So, that's why.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:50.070
He's a vampire-loving misanthrope.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.870
I do hope he recovers someday.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:01.540
Killing isn't the only thing you're good at.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:06.510
I need these skills to live among humans.

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:10.510
You get to see amazing things
when you live as long as me.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.760
I want to see even more.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.730
You're a vampire. Why do you seem happy?

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:19.350
What about you? You're still human.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.400
Huh?

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:24.650
I mean how you feel.
Those little ones are the same way.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:30.490
Kurusu's still got humanity left in him, too.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:35.620
What's the difference between
humans and vampires?

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:39.920
Whether they've gotten sick of being alive.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:44.550
Animals eat, sleep, make babies, and die.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.210
That's their whole lives.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:52.800
But humans have made all
kinds of fun things apart from that.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:57.520
Songs, plays, dances, and motion pictures.

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:01.020
Who knows what we'll be able to see next?

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:07.900
Isn't it fascinating?

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:09.030
Yeah.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.130
I just need to tell you?

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:36.260
All right.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:46.610
Wake up, it's time for your tea.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:54.360
Do you prefer to pour your milk
before your tea, or after?

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:57.580
My time is finally close at hand.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.880
I'll kill you next time.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:10.170
Oh, no, that won't do.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.340
The show is about to start.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.600
I...

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:26.860
You shouldn't move.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:31.190
I tried to stop the bleeding,
but you're losing a lot of blood.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.740
I didn't know.

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:41.330
I had no idea you were a vampire.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.660
You wouldn't have believed me anyway.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:51.210
This world is too harsh
for vampires to go on living in.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:54.470
We can't walk in the sunlight.

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:59.560
Our bodies don't age, so we
always have to fear exposure.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:03.560
But we have no choice
but to go on living as we are.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:09.520
As a result, our souls become unable
to keep up with our immortal bodies.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:13.440
The older a vampire gets,
the more prone they are to depression.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:17.780
They become like invalids and stay in the dark.

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:21.830
They stay in one place for centuries.

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:26.750
They grow exhausted of living in this world.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.460
However,

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:32.210
by playing many different people on stage,

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:35.590
while acting out fictional lives,

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:38.010
I die.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:43.520
Maybe that catharsis is what
enables me to stay somewhat sane.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:56.490
We belong in fairy tales.

00:11:56.490 --> 00:12:01.740
The world will keep being made
more modern and more rational.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.830
But that future world

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:09.500
has no place for us denizens of fairy tales.

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:15.880
Hey, doesn't it seem like Ascra
was mixed with the blood from Yokohama?

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:20.140
Oh, the stuff in Yoshiwara.
I'm surprised you knew.

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:21.890
Is that true?

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:23.100
Yes.

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.810
The vampire couple we dealt with in Kayabacho

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:30.100
must also have become addicted
to Ascra in exchange for pleasure.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:34.860
It turns humans into vampires
and vampires into addicts.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.990
Ascra must be a poison, huh?

00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:41.320
It can also be a medicine
for us in the right doses.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.910
Poison is poison. It doesn't turn into medicine.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.870
Alchemy that turns poison into medicine:

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.250
That's what chemistry is, Suwa.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.080
Even the skunk balls--

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.790
Don't mention them!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.800
Just remembering makes my nose wrinkle.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:58.920
Why do vampires want Ascra so badly?

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:03.300
Because it gives them an ecstasy
similar to drinking blood.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.140
Because human blood is so difficult to get,

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:09.980
they sought out Ascra as a substitute.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.560
I had no idea.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:16.070
Records buried in the dark
never see the light of day.

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:19.490
We're right here, though.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:21.570
You're right.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:24.950
All of us are here

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:27.040
in present-day Tokyo.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:37.090
If the sun gets a little higher,
I'll burn to ashes.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:41.090
If the water rises, I'll drown.

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:44.470
I wonder which it will be.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:48.640
You talk about dying so casually.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:53.310
Probably because I'm tired of living
in this world with no place for me.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.690
You really are a kid.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:59.070
I'm much older than you.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:02.740
People who say they've gotten sick of living

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:05.700
are kids, no matter how old they are.

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:13.210
Don't make trouble for me like Shutaro.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:16.710
Shutaro? You mean him?

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:20.960
You see, life is...

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:27.260
Hey.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.180
Damn it!

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:40.900
Shutaro Kurusu!

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.490
Save this woman!

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:45.860
What's wrong?

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:47.830
He's calling me.

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:48.780
Who is?

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.870
Shh!

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:53.000
Tsukishima...

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.170
Aoi?!

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:57.580
If you rush out now, you'll burn to a crisp.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.340
Aoi is hurt in the Tsukishima Island base!

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:01.960
I have to save her right now!

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:06.840
That's easy to say, but it will
take a long time on foot.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:09.760
More than enough time for us to burn to ashes.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.770
If I could go faster...

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.350
Can this fly right now?

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:16.770
Not a chance.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:19.270
I haven't done an unmanned test flight yet,

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:23.070
and I still need to test how parts
will hold up in a manned flight!

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:25.610
But you're making it to fly, right?

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.410
Only theoretically!

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:28.910
Then let's fly!

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:31.490
You made it, Takeuchi, so it'll work!

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:34.460
I appreciate your confidence.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:35.910
Don't bother.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:38.250
I don't want to see grilled vamp--

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.420
I'm going.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:47.340
This improved sunblock can weaken
direct sunlight to a degree.

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:54.310
But don't forget that the heat will build up

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:57.480
and cause a chemical reaction
in your skin underneath.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:58.980
Right.

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:01.770
You look like those stuffy bastards.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:07.740
The vampire units' equipment makes sense
for vampires operating during the day.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:11.330
But the vampire inside
is basically in a steam bath,

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:14.750
so Suwa's right that it
will always be sweltering.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.370
If you're conscious.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.210
Yes.

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:20.540
Even with this flying machine,

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:26.050
you'll likely reach ignition temperature
before reaching Tsukishima from here.

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:27.470
So, it'll be close.

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:30.510
The rest will come down to luck.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:35.060
I don't pray, but we should
this time, just in case.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:39.060
You've got your pick of God,
Buddha, or King Enma.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.310
Which one?

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:42.230
All of them, please!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:48.030
Shutaro Kurusu is now setting out
to rescue Aoi Shirase!

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:49.200
Good luck.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:51.070
Don't fall on the way.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.200
Right!

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:01.130
We'll see him off from here.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.810
You're late.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:20.230
I believe I'm right on time.

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:22.190
We've been waiting quite a while.

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:24.190
We have indeed.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:28.650
Then pardon me, but it was
an unexpected summons.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.240
I do have a job to do.

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:35.200
I hope you understand that.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:38.080
Now, what do you want to discuss?

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:42.710
You're finished, Nakajima.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:47.550
This vampire disturbance
is too much for you, isn't it?

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:51.930
Is there a problem with
my vampire units' performance?

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:54.600
They're not <i>your </i>vampire units, are they?

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:58.600
We know that you aren't the one commanding them.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.180
Exactly.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:04.690
I hear it's an extremely clever
young British man named Rufus.

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:10.400
So, we've decided you should
step down and transfer all authority...

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.280
...to him.

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:21.500
So, you wavered, too?

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:26.170
I, Rufus Glenn, never waver.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:30.170
Not from the very beginning.

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:35.800
Nakajima, we'd like you to step down.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:38.180
A mere human

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:41.060
could never compete with Rufus Glenn!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:55.280
I suggest you watch me become
king from someplace quiet.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:58.160
"And they all lived happily ever after."

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:10.050
Once upon a time, I, too, had a family.

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:13.010
I had a father, a mother,

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:15.300
and a little brother.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:18.010
But only I ended up like this.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:25.310
You know, the person who made me a vampire
stopped drinking blood after that.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:29.110
Out of the guilt she felt
for making me a vampire.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:36.780
I think she's the only vampire
I know of who died of starvation.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:43.580
No matter how much I offered
her blood, she wouldn't drink.

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:47.750
Then, when she died, she smiled and said,

00:19:47.750 --> 00:19:50.630
"I'm already full."

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:54.470
Hey.

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:57.430
Why do you think we're alive?

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.980
What is that thing?

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:11.820
Aoi!

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:24.750
Aoi!

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:29.710
She's not dead yet,

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:32.920
but she's still lost
a dangerous amount of blood.

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:34.800
Get her out of here quickly.

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:37.670
I'll do that.

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:39.050
And you?

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:44.350
On my own, I can manage as long
as a cloud hides the sun.

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:45.430
But...

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:49.230
Take care of Juliet, Romeo.

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:52.190
It's nothing.

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:53.480
Get going.

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.740
Take care.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.880
He really flew!

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.970
It's ridiculous, but...

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:25.390
Yes, it's just like... a fairy tale.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:33.860
Now, Rufus, it's time for act two.

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:56.380
Aoi, I'll save you.

00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:59.630
I'll protect you no matter what!

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:03.390
Shutaro... promise...

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:06.220
Yes, I promise.

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:46.980
King of Fools
